If the issue is the sprite losing its instance, you could correct it by checking if the sprite exists in the update cycle and end the update if it is missing.
Something like :
JavaScript:
const update = () => {
    if (!sprite || !sprite.parent) {
        return;
    }

    sprite.x = Graphics.width - (sprite.width/2) - offsetX;
    textSprite.x = 0;
    textSprite.y = 0;
    //rest of the code
This should handle the issue.

